From 0eb6624ce8b3ad9b1b126080bef3d342d556cadb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: praveen <praveenkumar.shanmugam@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:55:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] GPUOP-1133: Implement gpuagent_mock watcher

gpuagent_mock gets the smi-watcher event thread (1 s timer, tick plan,
synthetic FAST/SLOW/POWER sweep, DB update task, enqueue-only full frames),
the GPUWatchSubscribe IPC handler with queue attach, power view rebuild and
inactive cleanup (mirroring amdsmi), and the shared smi-power thread,
started from smi_init and joined first in smi_teardown.

Synthetic values are deterministic and monotonic per GPU: POWER
accumulation counter +1 per read, energy += power x period, residency +1
every 10 reads, power 300 + gpu + (n % 50) W, timestamps from
CLOCK_MONOTONIC; FAST GPU_CLOCK = 1000 + sweep seq, UBB power on every FAST
sweep (1 s floor, carried forward); SLOW ECC_CORRECT_TOTAL = slow seq.

Test knobs: AGA_MOCK_POWER_NA_FIELDS, AGA_MOCK_WATCH_READ_DELAY_US,
AGA_MOCK_WATCH_SWEEP_DELAY_MS (per GPU sweep sleep, + 100 ms per GPU on
slow ticks) and AGA_MOCK_WATCH_TRACE_READS.

Cleanup releases a failed stream from every watch it is on: the gRPC
thread sets write_failed concurrently, so smi_watch_sub_reap can report
only some of a multi-watch stream's pairs and the rest would keep a
pointer to the freed client context.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
